course: dictionary
lesson: 4599
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. A hermit is a person who chooses to live alone, away from other people. But «Picture a beach where hermit crabs line up by size» shows a different kind of hermit, an animal.
explain: Use the clues around the word to decide. «A hermit crab protects its soft, curled body inside an empty sea snail shell» tells you the hermit is a crab, because it lives inside a shell. Ask yourself: does this fit a person or an animal?
explain: Words often join up to make a new meaning. «Live like a hermit» means to live alone, away from people. «Hermit crab» is a special name for one kind of crab, so the first word does not mean a person there.
fact: A hermit is a person who chooses to live alone, away from other people.
fact: Some hermits lived alone in caves, deserts or huts to pray, often for religious reasons.
fact: A hermit crab is a crab that lives inside an empty shell of another sea animal.
fact: A hermit crab moves into a bigger shell as it grows.
fact: Someone who hardly ever goes out may be jokingly called a hermit.
exercise: «A hermit crab protects its soft, curled body inside an empty sea snail shell.» What kind of animal is a hermit crab? | A person who lives alone | A snail with a hard shell | A bird that nests in trees | *A crab that lives in an empty shell
exercise: «Hermit crabs sometimes queue by size and swap shells one after another.» Why do hermit crabs swap shells? | *Because they grow and need a bigger shell | To paint the shells | To keep the shells clean | To catch fish for dinner
exercise: Ben says, «I have turned into a hermit since I stopped going out to play.» What does he mean? | *He hardly goes out or sees other people | He has become a monk | He lives in a cave in the desert | He is a great fan of crabs
test: «A hermit crab has ten legs, but only six are easy to see.» Why are the other four hard to see? | They are missing | *They are small and hidden inside the shell | They are long and thin | They are painted gold
test: «The hermit lived in a hut in the desert and prayed every day.» Which meaning of hermit fits here? | A crab that lives in a shell | A kind of shop that sells shells | A sea snail | *A person who lives alone to pray
exam: In the story, the old hermit in the woods gave the lost boy a warm drink. Who is the hermit? | A hut used for storing tools | *A person who lives alone, away from other people | A sea snail with a hard shell | A crab that lives in a shell
